<%= render layout: "shared/modal", locals: { title: "What are meetups?" } do %>
  <article class="flex flex-col gap-y-8">
    <section>
      <p>Post a meetup:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
        <li>when you are free to do something, but not sure whom to do it with, or</li>
        <li>when its details are finalized after voting on the meetup idea.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section class="flex flex-col gap-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">For example:</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
        <li>Grabbing 🍔 food / ☕️ coffee</li>
        <li>🎲 Playing board games</li>
        <li>🥘 Cooking together</li>
        <li>🏀 Sports / Exercise</li>
        <li>📚 Study session / 💻 Coworking</li>
        <li>🍿 Going to the cinema</li>
        <li>👋 Hanging out</li>
        <li>⏰ Anything spontaneous</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section class="flex flex-col gap-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">What if I can't host it?</h2>
      <p>
        You should still post a meetup and say that you are "up to hang out". And in the description, you can write the friend whom you would like to host the meetup.
      </p>
      <p>
        For example, a friend of mine was "up for coworking" but his place was very small, so he wrote down in the description: "Oscar's place?" and invited me to RSVP.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="flex flex-col gap-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">What happens when I post a meetup?</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
        <li>Only the friends you invite can see and respond to it.</li>
        <li>For each of the invitees, a notification will be sent out in the form of push or email notification.</li>
        <li>When someone joins, you will get a push notification (if enabled).</li>
        <li>You will be able to see how many people have seen and said yes to your meetup post, so you can decide whether you should go through with it.</li>
        <li>If it actually happens and has more than 2 people (including you), it will be automatically turned into a memory the next day; you can then upload photos.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section class="flex flex-col gap-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">What is the difference between ideas and meetups?</h2>
      <p>An idea is a good starting point to make a meetup happen; this type of meetup is planned. People can pitch in their preferences and vote on the details of the meetup.</p>
      <p>A meetup is either planned or spontaneous. A planned meetup most likely will happen because it's been discussed. A spontaneous meetup is made last minutes, so there's a higher chance of people not seeing / joining.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
<% end %>
